From b3005469a5d1a3c2da9b43e3a7e0d40fab577175 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: D313373 <d.1337.edu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 01:58:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Split script vs agent page-map pipelines and restore native
 directory navigation.

Script runs use locator-only resolution with optional PageMapExtractor fallback (non-greedy, timed out), while agent runs keep APC with interactive-only dedupe capped at 64 nodes. Native execution activates the tab at run start and uses forceActivation for directory clicks and type focus; CDP paths are unchanged. Directory navigate prefers trusted click, then referrer LoadURL, then direct load.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
